    "terminal_reason": "Charged honestly, the policy NEVER pays on a single query in any world: the scan that produces the ordering costs more than the ordering saves, which is exactly the 'explicit retrieval moves rather than removes cost' risk #214 section 6 names. It pays only as an AMORTISED preparation, and the break-even is now a number rather than a hope: {'RARE_DECISIVE': 2, 'COMMON_DECISIVE': 4, 'RARE_DECOY': 5, 'TYPE_DECOY': None}. That is the same shape main already uses -- ExtractionIndex charges build_work separately from query work with object-bound validity -- so the mechanism inherits an existing discipline instead of needing a new one. Where the break-even is None the scan is never repaid at any horizon and the honest reading for that world is NO_LIFETIME_PAYBACK.",
